=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2.$ Applying the above formula with $x=2$ and $h=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{g(2+4)-g(2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-8}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47387/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342037/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6456cccc-0cc9-5ecf-92ce-2dbbeede2972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342037/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e61e8ba-c70b-5c12-8e33-d8d353588f6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342037/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-342037/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342037" :question/id #uuid "9ed1d3b2-7869-51db-81ee-b2ccc32ccf11" :question/math-academy-id "q-342037" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/c51e6206f77b63181f6c9f67b116ba5c0024886c061e8c15fe10edab87c87e03.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3.$ Applying the above formula with $x=3$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+2)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342037/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "03b603af-12f4-59db-a7d3-a99f86e9ce26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "80a175c0-a8bd-56ca-b5e9-cabe2e658a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "589c5620-d46d-5183-8359-a008cd7a3a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "0ce9ce65-6cee-5e11-a2c9-aee114094221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "ed81ae3b-2303-536f-8eeb-79c0ef67e4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1da1d1b3-3abd-5982-a4ce-de54ef5a7583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47388/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-47388/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-47388/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-47388/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-47388/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-47388/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47388" :question/id #uuid "209d8d0b-5f16-5023-9c47-f445a99d48ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-47388" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/1534153e6a5d79400a038849b48583d2ec9a62db1fc1f52a491b751e46861f51.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.$ Applying the above formula with $x=0$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0) & ≈\\frac{g(0+2)-g(0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2)-g(0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-10}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47388/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342040/field-1/631278020d4feb6e6637bbf6f3aedefe7a2af6275b863fcbb6dd29a701c97b2d" :answer/id #uuid "b923956b-e419-5ddd-b919-0bd30634ed97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "110" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342040/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "45c82cc2-134c-5f6d-b9d2-ea921d99cf28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342040/field-1/631278020d4feb6e6637bbf6f3aedefe7a2af6275b863fcbb6dd29a701c97b2d" :answer-field/choices ["q-342040/field-1/631278020d4feb6e6637bbf6f3aedefe7a2af6275b863fcbb6dd29a701c97b2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342040" :question/id #uuid "c44cb097-7152-5126-bd0e-9033f85fd6ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-342040" :question/problem "A hiker’s elevation was recorded over time for $6$ hours, starting from time $t=0$ hours. The following table shows the elevation $E(t)$, in meters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $E(t)$ | $0$ | $200$ | $310$ | $395$ | $450$ | $525$ | $600$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of elevation at time $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=1,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} meters per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{E}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{E(t+h)-E(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{E(1+1)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{E(2)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{310-200}{1} \\\\  & =110.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=1$ the rate of change was approximately $110$ meters per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342040/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection/dc3c80070fec9987e8dae42ad7155c5e469a69d93b674969ddf8a3a542d8e83c" :answer/id #uuid "f9e75a82-4cbb-54e8-876d-0ef10e4cdf74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection/1fb9d0de8c47026863d2ae88645bfb54e0edd86bc5477f245e1f20a2e7562037" :answer/id #uuid "b45839c3-7499-59ab-8faa-e0d148ee2a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection/a9d9ef13339c473e340bcd6061ee0a4182f3b24f18397c0583abacc919f5ebea" :answer/id #uuid "0832afa2-2713-598b-924f-00733470ebe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection/36b5f29c41a3e4c05548cafde6b2d92e2bfeca59315548320be018d54169a93f" :answer/id #uuid "d2a88dd3-6060-544d-ba70-4ef6c2975bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection/207f111664567feab18a6110770889b6d1683b9bcc64093b67b400df390f642a" :answer/id #uuid "0b0ebc80-d294-5f1b-bd94-0dd7b0bf031e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "997ef771-7667-56c3-b41b-61101242d3e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47378/selection/a9d9ef13339c473e340bcd6061ee0a4182f3b24f18397c0583abacc919f5ebea" :answer-field/choices ["q-47378/selection/dc3c80070fec9987e8dae42ad7155c5e469a69d93b674969ddf8a3a542d8e83c" "q-47378/selection/1fb9d0de8c47026863d2ae88645bfb54e0edd86bc5477f245e1f20a2e7562037" "q-47378/selection/a9d9ef13339c473e340bcd6061ee0a4182f3b24f18397c0583abacc919f5ebea" "q-47378/selection/36b5f29c41a3e4c05548cafde6b2d92e2bfeca59315548320be018d54169a93f" "q-47378/selection/207f111664567feab18a6110770889b6d1683b9bcc64093b67b400df390f642a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47378" :question/id #uuid "e5d32ddd-0763-54da-be13-1a93cdb99dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-47378" :question/problem "Andrey wants to estimate his running speed. Andrey's friend Max takes note of Andrey's position while he is on the track. Max's observations are given in the table below, where $s(t)$ is the distance covered, measured in meters, $t$ seconds after Andrey started running.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $4$ | $9$ | $15$ | $20$ | $27$ |\n\nApproximate Andrey's speed at the point where $t=6$ seconds using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{s(6+2)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(8)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=6$ Andrey's speed is approximately $2.5\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47378/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection/bda41b03c64d85b97d1552c02f98a4af11f8d1eaef34484f26af68f949e7e27c" :answer/id #uuid "c394eb42-685b-5eaf-a02e-adebe4bdc3f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$32$ eggs per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection/2a66c3f98841084bea10f61955f0c1610918bd4b38d273e8abdef91256a05fda" :answer/id #uuid "b7ac46d4-8131-5c08-a12d-cb02a4370dff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27$ eggs per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection/0448d97e449fa5ac2892b5f1a522aa2dbf2d9b0ae2c4f580af7d5fd578a239af" :answer/id #uuid "fdc19acb-e216-5b95-8e16-d824106d1c77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$38$ eggs per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection/b7a3161788f6c3287a17e059e59b8f51ac644f3cd93392e7bf36bbfbbada6e7e" :answer/id #uuid "9a0cebb3-43c1-5e78-9114-f9d0b18087a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$43$ eggs per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection/6c82adffa2374a20215fabe789825e84cfcd800128c0cd360912b8ea68638a09" :answer/id #uuid "2644bfd1-3e41-5e9e-bd5f-d3d0f0396273" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$45$ eggs per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26f24659-ac60-59c1-b329-93f9a812b7f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71925/selection/b7a3161788f6c3287a17e059e59b8f51ac644f3cd93392e7bf36bbfbbada6e7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-71925/selection/bda41b03c64d85b97d1552c02f98a4af11f8d1eaef34484f26af68f949e7e27c" "q-71925/selection/2a66c3f98841084bea10f61955f0c1610918bd4b38d273e8abdef91256a05fda" "q-71925/selection/0448d97e449fa5ac2892b5f1a522aa2dbf2d9b0ae2c4f580af7d5fd578a239af" "q-71925/selection/b7a3161788f6c3287a17e059e59b8f51ac644f3cd93392e7bf36bbfbbada6e7e" "q-71925/selection/6c82adffa2374a20215fabe789825e84cfcd800128c0cd360912b8ea68638a09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71925" :question/id #uuid "eb0fa8c3-bd0e-5154-8c3c-3cb2dfba2a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-71925" :question/problem "The total number of eggs laid by a pen of chickens on a farm is given by the function $e(t),$ where $t$ is the number of days since the chickens arrived on the farm. The values of $e(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $e(t)$ | $20$ | $45$ | $77$ | $117$ | $160$ | $195$ |\n\nApproximate the rate at which eggs are laid at the $4$th day using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{e}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{e(t+h)-e(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=4.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{e(4+1)-e(4)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{e(5)-e(4)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{160-117}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{1} \\\\  & =43.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=4$ the rate at which eggs are laid is approximately $43$ eggs per day." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71925/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71925"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342038/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0f2ba0ab-900f-5b23-afe3-8e9ebaca0f07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342038/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "ba95476f-1be3-51f2-b940-a27e388ae9d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342038/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7a6b482-53c5-577a-8e9e-c09454d3673f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342038/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-342038/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-342038/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342038" :question/id #uuid "70e8b70f-3021-53a3-b823-74d92203bf17" :question/math-academy-id "q-342038" :question/problem "The volume of water in a tank was recorded over time for $25$ minutes, starting from time $t=0$ minutes. The following table shows the volume $V(t)$, in liters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V(t)$ | $120$ | $150$ | $165$ | $180$ | $215$ | $240$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of volume at time $t=5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=5,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} liters per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{V(t+h)-V(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{V(5+5)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{V(10)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{165-150}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=5$ the rate of change was approximately $3$ liters per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342038/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-47380"] :question/problem "The function $g(s)$ describes the amount of fuel, in liters, remaining in Samuel's car after driving $s$ miles. The values of $g(s)$ for different values of $s$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $s$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(s)$ | $15$ | $13.5$ | $12.1$ | $9.4$ | $8.2$ | $6.6$ | $4.8$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change in the fuel volume when $s=8$ miles using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(s)≈\\frac{g(s+h)-f(s)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $s=8.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{g(8+2)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.6-8.2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.6}{2} \\\\  & =-0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $s=8$ the rate at which the fuel is changing is approximately $-0.8\\,\\text{liters/mile}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-342075/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc" :answer/id #uuid "ca988ad1-34e6-5afc-a468-61832cf2a285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342075/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "257cf450-86c1-5a9d-987c-e360972cb657" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342075/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc" :answer-field/choices ["q-342075/field-1/acb11913e40f66990ef37d5f8d45159f9639ad6d7e0b6d5fbf3b8692ed1dfedc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342075" :question/id #uuid "408ca6b1-3ddb-58f1-8b96-44e416ee959f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342075" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/d84ba0a07821011be4cf5958af44ea73e97493c5a796a0324b068fe2adca8a12.png)\n\nA car is using petrol as it travels. The graph of the amount of petrol $P(d)$, in liters, remaining in the fuel tank after traveling a distance of $d$ miles is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the amount of petrol at $d=150$ using a forward difference with step size $h=50.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the amount of petrol decreases.\n\nAfter traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is {{field-1}} liters per mile." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(d)≈\\frac{P(d+h)-P(d)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the distance $d=150$ with step size $h=50.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(150) & ≈\\frac{P(150+50)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(200)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-30}{50} \\\\  & =-0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is $-0.4$ liters per mile." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342075/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-313343/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "9caecc5d-8440-591f-94ab-128cafe9ec7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313343/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "e59dc82f-546e-5054-bfaf-c42e76ef5fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-313343/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1f5b66-8134-5091-8a35-8e0a994c04cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-313343/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-313343/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-313343/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-313343" :question/id #uuid "2d82fcd9-f4c5-508c-af92-d0f336d3879f" :question/math-academy-id "q-313343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/204afb23fc438b047c72d6233b59b70c4741ee16a30a57c084682a3d14fd2188.png)\n\nA thin soap film is stretching over time. The graph of its surface area $A(t)$, in square centimeters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the surface area at $t=2$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nAfter $2$ minutes, the surface area increases at a rate of {{field-1}} ${\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{A(t+h)-A(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=2$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{A(2+2)-A(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{A(4)-A(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-10}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $2$ minutes, the surface area changes at a rate of approximately $15\\text{ }{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-313343/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-313343"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342079/field-1/008b962e8dba6a793a19582d7b90d25ecc915fb39cdb8821fa797599cabe57ab" :answer/id #uuid "b29d6424-c745-5f0f-9f1d-a47b5c80cbc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342079/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a20db44-2111-5ec2-9b1b-28d00d485b8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342079/field-1/008b962e8dba6a793a19582d7b90d25ecc915fb39cdb8821fa797599cabe57ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-342079/field-1/008b962e8dba6a793a19582d7b90d25ecc915fb39cdb8821fa797599cabe57ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342079" :question/id #uuid "cfa3059e-2dcb-5fa2-abb3-d25cbe930e7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342079" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/846fc347c71ada4c01a5a85aabd0722203b84edbafcbe462064ae31d1cf2adbb.png)\n\nA drone is descending toward the ground. The graph of its height $H(t)$, in meters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the height at $t=9$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the height decreases.\n\nAfter $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is {{field-1}} meters per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{H}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{H(t+h)-H(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=9$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{′}(9) & ≈\\frac{H(9+2)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(11)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-80}{2} \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is $-40$ meters per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342079/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342079"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186092665 :question/answer-fields 17592186090455] {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/a0fdcfa6217fc812079e529d1975e6fe131c7e8147b591e55d4bb9b697e66a35" :answer/id #uuid "fb74c996-e28a-5854-90b8-f16feb27f8fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/8eda4ff13dd1fd99f50f646a250f404c35fb30750b2a55554b163c11389bf872" :answer/id #uuid "1d458ed0-df6b-58ec-8fe5-0ce3477b3bd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/dbad8309c9b344f94cf2226178ee23e9c35c70d18fdcd459bd24d5547497280d" :answer/id #uuid "d8a99d56-eb10-533c-b9fa-bdc7b622da1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37.5\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/a45822e97dafe75bf3d961cabcc542c29f7e3691aebaa0f01a0f2a672dc82065" :answer/id #uuid "3ba89f6c-4e74-58dc-925c-ad8541caf6cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/1ff676223d1adc172d0f24ff52cf1cb23bd779ea58f01369916774d7b32a1ce0" :answer/id #uuid "cb70e0ec-adee-58cc-8365-b9caa9350cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22" :answer-field/id #uuid "06c9aa36-4fd9-5e1c-a1fa-c68d14105427" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/a0fdcfa6217fc812079e529d1975e6fe131c7e8147b591e55d4bb9b697e66a35" :answer-field/choices ["q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/a0fdcfa6217fc812079e529d1975e6fe131c7e8147b591e55d4bb9b697e66a35" "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/8eda4ff13dd1fd99f50f646a250f404c35fb30750b2a55554b163c11389bf872" "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/dbad8309c9b344f94cf2226178ee23e9c35c70d18fdcd459bd24d5547497280d" "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/a45822e97dafe75bf3d961cabcc542c29f7e3691aebaa0f01a0f2a672dc82065" "q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22/1ff676223d1adc172d0f24ff52cf1cb23bd779ea58f01369916774d7b32a1ce0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-47383"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/4a7e89a828cbd660357d4834e0bcb9cb5c316dbe24419865206ba5f41872963d.png)\n\nThe power of a mobile phone emitter increases when the phone is switched on. The power output of the emitter after $t$ minutes is given by $W(t),$ where $W$ is measured in watts. The graph of $W(t)$ is shown above. \nApproximate the rate of increase in the power of the emitter when $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{W(1+2)-W(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(3)-W(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{100-50}{2} \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $1$ minute, the power is increasing at a rate of approximately $25\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47383/selection/ma-v1/b06928bbae0e52267db576b4f157e487e2a3d36a8beeddebfb466d635e7dee22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-342080/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "fa218d2d-e025-53fe-ab29-dc986fde4c70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342080/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbeb63ae-4e3e-5c1a-9159-eb9d96349c78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342080/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-342080/field-1/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342080" :question/id #uuid "2642c08d-d846-51fe-9494-87c5a3d1bf87" :question/math-academy-id "q-342080" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/ae57faa04abd053e4a58d751cc084d58e07e84e0520c99a33a122f58dfd8f18c.png)\n\nA slice of jackfruit is placed in an air dryer. The graph of the moisture content $M(t)$, in percent, after $t$ hours is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the moisture content at $t=3$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the content decreases.\n\nAfter $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is {{field-1}} percent per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{M(3+2)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(5)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-40}{2} \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is $-10$ percent per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342080/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-151"] :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1.0$ | $-0.7$ | $-0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1.5$ | $2.1$ |\n\nApproximate  at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+1)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-0.3)-(-0.7)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.4}{1} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-152"] :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown below. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/3084d6ae67f37517f3d8ad0a9a62be05fe1906fcc2a24f69bd29a1e00dfd0373.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\frac{g(x+h) - g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4.$  Applying the above formula with $x=4$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+2)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-153"] :question/problem "The position of a race car along a straight track, measured in feet from the starting line, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $7$ | $12$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s'(t)$ at the time $t=0.1$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ns'(t) \\approx \\frac{s(t+h) - s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=0.1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(0.1) & ≈\\frac{s(0.1+0.1)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(0.2)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-3}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.1} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=0.1$ the velocity is approximately $40\\, \\textrm{ft}/\\textrm{s}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-154"] :question/problem "An oil tank has leaked $q(t)$ liters of oil after $t$ hours. The graph of $q(t)$ is shown below. Approximate the rate at which the oil is leaking from the tank when $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/b6c5286dae7e739a588173bad9c721ae34d07f86e455e44ec9f229628cf54211.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\nq'(t) \\approx \\frac{q(t+h) - q(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=1$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{q(1+1)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $1$ hour, the tank is leaking oil at a rate of approximately $1\\,\\textrm{liter}/ \\textrm{hour}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
